WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.160
A lump of grey flint.

2
00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:06.060
A steel striker hovers
over it, but never strikes.

3
00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:08.770
Is there warmth inside that stone already?

4
00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.790
Or does it have to be put there?

5
00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:13.280
Dickens builds Scrooge from cold.

6
00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:18.730
Frost on his head, "his thin lips
blue", "solitary as an oyster".

7
00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:22.240
By morning, the same figure
stands in warm light.

8
00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:25.390
A change overnight, or in him all along?

9
00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:29.260
In this mission, you'll take
apart Dickens's Stave 1 portrait,

10
00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:31.340
word by cold word.

11
00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:34.450
You'll track the signs of
change, stave by stave,

12
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.950
from Stave 2 to Stave 5.

13
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.880
And you'll weigh two views.

14
00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:41.180
Is the change too sudden to believe?

15
00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:43.150
Or does Dickens prepare it?

16
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:46.520
Your mission: decide if
the change came overnight,

17
00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:48.200
or was already in him.
